  "answer": "The goal was met: five settings on five different scenes failed on every repeat (S9, S12, S17, S24, S30). However, they mostly show VaVAM drifting out of its lane at small or zero perturbation, not failures caused by the bias and speed knobs. Two of the five (S9, S24) fail with no bias at recorded speed. Of the other three, S17 adds only speed (1.4x), and S12 and S30 add only +0.1 m of bias (at 1.0x and 1.2x). The planned corners (\u00b10.3 to \u00b10.5 m at 1.2 to 1.4x) were never run, so the study does not show how larger perception errors behave. With three runs per setting, each confirmed range only just clears 0.5, and the true rates could be anywhere from about half to always. All of S9 and S12's failures, and part of S17's, need caveats. In S9 and S12 every failure ended more than 3.5 m from the recorded path, so the rendering could play a part, although triage blamed the policy each time. One of S17's three failures involved a pedestrian, and fault there is unclear.",
